From: Gemini experiment archive <noreply@gemini-experiment.invalid>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: bypass RTC mode writes in the captured experiment

The wrapper can select recovery, fastboot or charging mode in RTC before
the low-level reset owner rejects a competing reset. Route experimental
restart requests directly through that existing owner with the ordinary
restart argument. Before takeover this preserves a normal reset path;
after takeover it parks without changing RTC mode or the owned deadline.
No new lock or reset implementation is introduced. Ordinary builds retain
the complete existing wrapper behavior.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic author, no DCO certification.
---
 drivers/watchdog/mediatek/wdk/wd_api.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/mediatek/wdk/wd_api.c b/drivers/watchdog/mediatek/wdk/wd_api.c
index 7043b25..58ac0f3 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/mediatek/wdk/wd_api.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/mediatek/wdk/wd_api.c
@@ -589,6 +589,12 @@ void arch_reset(char mode, const char *cmd)
 	int res = 0;
 	struct wd_api *wd_api = NULL;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MTK_A72_RECOVERY_DISCRIMINATOR
+	/* The low-level owner parks after takeover; never change RTC boot modes. */
+	wdt_arch_reset(1);
+	return;
+#endif
+
 	res = get_wd_api(&wd_api);
 	pr_alert("arch_reset: cmd = %s\n", cmd ? : "NULL");
 	dump_stack();
